    "title": "EFV neuropsychiatric toxicity: insomnia and vivid dreams",
    "message": "Guidelines list insomnia and related neuropsychiatric symptoms as EFV toxicities and recommend: if on EFV 600mg, lower to 400mg; if on EFV 400mg, reassure, and if symptoms persist, substitute EFV with DTG. Patient started TDF+3TC+EFV in February 2024 and now reports poor sleep and vivid dreams for several weeks. EFV is a well-established cause of these symptoms. No alternative cause is evident from the clinical notes, though anxiety or other psychosocial factors could contribute. The clinician's plan documents the complaints but does not include any management step such as dose reduction or substitution.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "If on EFV 600mg, reduce to 400mg. If already on 400mg, reassure and if symptoms persist, substitute EFV with DTG (or ATV/r if DTG contraindicated).",
