    "title": "Viral load 60 copies/mL: low-level viremia not addressed",
    "message": "Guidelines define viral suppression as plasma VL ≤200 copies/mL. Patient's last VL was 60 copies/mL on 2025-08-10, which is technically suppressed. However, guidelines acknowledge low-level viremia as a concern for subsequent virologic non-suppression. The clinician's plan does not document recognition of this low-level value or enhanced monitoring. No repeat VL is ordered despite the potential risk.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
